  "diagnosis": "attempt 2 was stopped by the wrapper at 'own RSS 32.4 GiB above 32.0 GiB' in 'truth', right after the moment observables, i.e. when f_pdf forked its 8 workers for the first DM-PDF pass. The guard sums the RSS of every process in the tree; a forked worker's RSS includes all of the parent's resident pages it shares copy-on-write, so the sum is ~ (1 + 8) x parent RSS + the workers' private memory. The parent then held the three fine bases (3 x 0.737 GB: W_y, W_tau [421 z, 10 bins, 75 shells, 106 ell] and the K tensors), the importance Jacobians, and heap left over from the basis build in the same process (basis parent peak 12.5 GiB): ~3.5-3.6 GiB x 9 = 32.4 GiB. The real (PSS) footprint was ~5-6 GB.",
  "fix": [
   "truth: one basis in memory at a time (FP: parity; HA, HM: production truths and the cross-basis checks), each deleted before the next; none at the DM-PDF / Mecke forks (f_pdf reads only g_E, gbar_E lazily from the basis file)",
   "sens / beyond / binning: the basis, Jacobians and 2-halo prefix sums are deleted before the DM-PDF forks",
   "params: fits -> DM-PDF / Mecke passes -> bootstrap pool, all before the basis and the H3 maps are loaded; only the imp__a2ii__* maps of sens.npz are read",
   "h_common.release(): gc + glibc malloc_trim(0) before every fork and between stages; h_common.mem() logs the parent RSS / PSS at every fork point (results/run_manifest.json: memory_checkpoints per stage)",
   "attempt 3 reruns prepare,truth,sens,params,beyond,binning in a fresh process and reuses the attempt-2 bases in /tmp/nagainis_halfdome_testH (sha256 / zip CRC / finiteness checked on maas; the basis code is unchanged), so no basis-build heap is carried into 'truth'"
